-- title:
--   The crossing model is not formally smooth over the base
-- statement:
--   Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain with the `IsDiscreteValuationRing` structure) and let $\varpi_0 \in A_0$ generate its maximal ideal, $\mathfrak m_{A_0} = (\varpi_0)$. Let $R$ be a noetherian local commutative ring and $j : A_0 \to R$ a ring homomorphism. Let $w$ be a natural number with $w \ge 1$. Suppose given a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak m_R$-adic completion of $R$ onto the quotient of the ring of formal power series in two variables, indexed by `Fin 2`, over the $\mathfrak m_{A_0}$-adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$ of $A_0$, by the principal ideal generated by $X_0 X_1 - C\big(\varpi_0^{\,w}\big)$, where $\varpi_0^{\,w}$ is taken in $\widehat{A_0}$ through the canonical map and $C$ is the constant-coefficient inclusion. Suppose moreover that $e$ matches constants with constants: for every $a \in A_0$, the image under $e$ of the canonical image of $j(a)$ in the completion of $R$ is the class of the constant power series $C(a)$, again with $a$ viewed in $\widehat{A_0}$. Then $j$ is not formally smooth in the sense of `RingHom.FormallySmooth`.
--
--   This is the statement that an ordinary double point, in the shape $\widehat{A_0}[[u,v]]/(uv - \varpi_0^{\,w})$ with $w \ge 1$, is not a formally smooth point of the base discrete valuation ring; the hypothesis $w \ge 1$ is essential, since for $w = 0$ the equation $uv = 1$ defines a smooth torus. It is used to show that the nodes of the semistable model of the full-level modular curve over a tame base lie outside the smooth locus, in the three results on node charts and adic completions of stalks of the normal model that cite it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_RingHom_not_formallySmooth_of_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_crossingModel.lean

import Mathlib

